/.lake
/MathlibTest/.lake
*.olean
*.ilean
*.trace
/build
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# latexmk artifacts beside the metatheory write-up. They are inert for the Lean
# build, but any untracked file makes `git status` dirty, and the benchmark
# harness stamps that into every run's metadata as `crush_dirty=true` -- which
# marks the run as not reconstructible from a commit. Scoped to this directory
# so the patterns cannot swallow a real file elsewhere.
/Crush/Metatheory/Formalization/*.aux
/Crush/Metatheory/Formalization/*.fdb_latexmk
/Crush/Metatheory/Formalization/*.fls
/Crush/Metatheory/Formalization/*.log
/Crush/Metatheory/Formalization/*.out
/Crush/Metatheory/Formalization/*.toc

# Benchmark run output. Every run writes a timestamped directory here, so
# leaving these unignored means running the benchmark dirties the tree and the
# next run stamps `crush_dirty=true` into its own metadata -- measuring makes
# the next measurement look unreconstructible. The recorded archive is tracked
# and stays; tracked files ignore these patterns regardless.
/BenchmarkResults/*
!/BenchmarkResults/recorded/
